   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="address">
                    <ab>
                        <address>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_CHE_ZURI_06">Universitätstrasse 38, I</name>
                            </addrLine>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_CHE_ZURI">Zurich</name>
                            </addrLine>
                        </address>
                    </ab>
                </div>
                <div type="mainBody">
                    <p>Dear <name type="person" key="weav76">Miss Weaver</name>: I think it useless to give you the names of booksellers in Italy. At the present rate of exchange (40) <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">
                            <rs type="work" key="W_APORTRAIT">my novel</rs>
                        </seg> would sell at about 16 lire! I may say that it is almost impossible for any English novel published at 6/- to compete with continental novels selling at 3 or 4 francs. I hope you got in <seg xml:id="seg2" type="note-anchor">some other subscriptions</seg> from friends of mine. Would it be possible to have the copies of your paper sent out (at least to subscribers here and to me) every month instead of every two months? Will you please send copies also (from February issue on) to: <name type="person" key="murr62">Mrs Murray</name>, 10 Fairview Road, Church Road, Dublin. The amount of subscription to be charged to my account. I hope <name type="person" key="poun85">Mr Pound</name> is not ill. It is a long time since I heard from him.</p>
                    <closer>
                        <salute>With kind regards</salute>
                        <salute>sincerely yours</salute>
                        <signed>
                            <name type="person" key="joyc82">James Joyce</name>
                        </signed>
                        <dateline>
                            <date when="1918-02-26">26/2/918</date>
                        </dateline>
                    </closer>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">
                    <name type="work" key="W_APORTRAIT">A Portrait of the Artist as a Young Man</name>.</note>
                <note xml:id="note2" target="#seg2" type="commentary">Subscriptions for <name type="work" key="W_THEEGOIST">The Egoist</name>. In his <rs type="letter" key="L_68456">letter to Harriet Weaver of <date when="1918-02-04">4 February 1918</date>
                    </rs>, JJ wrote: “I have got some subscriptions for your journal here. They will reach you from various friends of mine in Switzerland”.</note>
            </div>
      </body>
   </text>
